Initialize headless print state independently of allocator contents.

The current pinned fork defaults Print's constructor but leaves printer mode,
plate origin and FakeWipeTower scalar/Eigen members uninitialized. Android's
standalone adapter has no GUI setup pass; these values select the wipe-tower
algorithm and enter geometry calculations. Fresh prints must start as non-Bambu
with a zero plate origin and an empty tower, with explicit setters still taking
precedence. Eigen default construction does not zero its coefficients.

This is an Android runtime fix with its own recorded patch identity. It does
not republish or alter the browser/server engine. It was audited against the
current source, not copied from the retired v2.3.2 patch set. The retired tower
layer-counter change is unnecessary on this pin: generate() sets it before
active reads; the earlier save_on_last_wipe() call is under #if 0.

Retire this patch when the selected upstream initializes these fields itself.
The internal defaults probe constructs actual engine objects over several
nonzero byte patterns and checks defaults plus explicit setter behavior.

---
diff --git a/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp b/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp
